{"name":"Phlox","hex":"#df00ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Phlox","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Polemoniaceae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Phlox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Phlox","blocks":[{"text":"Phlox is a genus of 68 species of perennial and annual plants in the family Polemoniaceae. They are found mostly in North America in diverse habitats from alpine tundra to open woodland and prairie. Some flower in spring, others in summer and fall. Flowers may be pale blue, violet, pink, bright red, or white. Many are fragrant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Phlox_glaberrima.jpg/330px-Phlox_glaberrima.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phlox","wikidata":"Q652016"},{"title":"Phlox (Star Trek)","blocks":[{"text":"Phlox is a fictional character, played by John Billingsley, in the television series Star Trek: Enterprise. Set in the 22nd century in the science fiction Star Trek universe, he is the physician aboard the first human Warp 5 capable starship, Enterprise (NX-01), commanded by Captain Jonathan Archer. Phlox first appears in the premiere episode, \"Broken Bow\" (2001), marking the franchise's introduction of the Denobulan race."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/Phlox_%28Star_Trek%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phlox_(Star_Trek)","wikidata":"Q2600949"},{"title":"Shades of purple","blocks":[{"text":"There are numerous variations of the color purple, a sampling of which is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shades_of_Purple.svg/330px-Shades_of_Purple.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_purple","wikidata":"Q7